# Plan: Learn Python in 1 Week

## Overview
This plan aims to provide a comprehensive introduction to Python programming within one week. By following this structured approach, you'll cover the basics of Python syntax, data structures, control flow, and essential libraries, preparing you for more advanced topics.

## Prerequisites
| Requirement | Why It's Needed |
|---|---|
| Basic Computer Skills | To navigate your development environment and run code |
| Internet Access | To access learning resources and tools |

## Learning Path
1. **Python Basics** — Understand the fundamentals of Python syntax, variables, and data types.
2. **Control Flow** — Learn how to use conditional statements and loops in Python.
3. **Data Structures** — Explore lists, tuples, dictionaries, and sets.
4. **Functions** — Create reusable blocks of code with functions.
5. **Modules & Libraries** — Understand how to import and use external libraries.

## Step-by-step Plan

### Phase 1 — Foundation
- [ ] Install Python on your computer (use [Python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/))
- [ ] Set up a code editor or IDE (e.g., [Visual Studio Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/) with the Python extension)
- [ ] Learn basic syntax and data types by completing exercises from [Codecademy's Python course](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-python-3)

### Phase 2 — Setup & Configuration
- [ ] Practice writing simple scripts to reinforce your understanding of variables, control flow, and functions.
- [ ] Explore built-in Python data structures like lists, tuples, dictionaries, and sets through interactive exercises on [LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/) or [HackerRank](https://www.hackerrank.com/domains/tutorials/10-days-of-python)

### Phase 3 — Execution
- [ ] Dive into modules and libraries by working on projects that utilize external packages. For example, use the `requests` library to fetch data from an API.
- [ ] Learn about file handling in Python by creating a script that reads from and writes to files.
- [ ] Explore more advanced control flow with list comprehensions and generator expressions.

### Phase 4 — Launch / Completion
- [ ] Review all topics covered during the week, focusing on areas where you struggled or found challenging.
- [ ] Take a short quiz or test to assess your understanding of Python basics. Use resources like [Khan Academy's Python quizzes](https://www.khanacademy.org/computing/computer-science/cs101/python).
- [ ] Start working on small projects or contribute to open-source projects to apply what you've learned.

## Estimated Timeline
| Phase | Estimated Duration |
|---|---|
| Phase 1 — Foundation | 2 days |
| Phase 2 — Setup & Configuration | 3 days |
| Phase 3 — Execution | 2 days |
| Phase 4 — Launch | 1 day |

## Key Resources
- **Python.org** — Official documentation and tutorials.
- **Codecademy's Python course** — Interactive lessons with exercises.
- **LeetCode** — Practice coding problems.
- **HackerRank** — Additional practice and challenges.
- **Khan Academy** — Quizzes to test your knowledge.

